                <pb facs="0152" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 80.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 285.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 9, 1870</date>. (Received September
                    22.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inclose you herewith
                    the proclamation of the government of the national defense, together with
                    certain decrees issued yesterday, and appearing in the official journal this
                    morning. You will perceive that an election is ordered for the 16th proximo for
                    members of a national constituent assembly, to consist of one hundred and fifty
                    delegates.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>



